# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your Supabase project's values
# (Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard).
# Until these are set, the app runs entirely on a localStorage-backed mock
# data layer — see src/lib/supabaseClient.ts.
#
# Once these are set, the app requires Google sign-in (src/components/AuthGate.ts)
# from one of the two whitelisted accounts in src/lib/auth.ts. Before that will
# work, enable the Google provider under Supabase Dashboard -> Authentication ->
# Providers, and run supabase/migrations/0002_tighten_rls.sql in the SQL editor.
# No extra env vars are needed for OAuth — Supabase manages the Google client
# ID/secret, and the redirect URL is computed from window.location.origin.
#
# Deploying to a new domain (e.g. a new Cloudflare Pages/Workers URL)? Add that
# domain to Supabase Dashboard -> Authentication -> URL Configuration -> Redirect
# URLs (e.g. https://your-domain.dev/**). Without it, sign-in silently redirects
# back to whatever domain is set as the Site URL instead of the one you're on.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
